# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PREVIEW OVERRIDES
# Loaded by Vite on top of the base .env when building with `--mode preview`
# (see package.json's `build:preview`/`deploy:preview` scripts). Only values
# that differ from production belong here -- everything else falls through
# to .env. This is what lets a PR's preview build call a sibling app's own
# preview deployment instead of production; see docs/decisions/ for the
# cross-app-preview ADR.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

PUBLIC_SOURCES_API_HOST=https://sources-preview.tabitha.bible
PUBLIC_TARGETS_API_HOST=https://targets-preview.tabitha.bible

# Blanked so Auth.js skips the redirect proxy here: this preview build is served from its own
# stable custom domain, whose callback is registered directly on the Google OAuth client, so it
# can complete the flow itself rather than bouncing through production. The proxy stays set in
# .env for production, which still serves per-commit *.workers.dev previews that cannot register
# a redirect URI of their own.
OAUTH_REDIRECT_PROXY_URL=
